+      "Socks, gloves and shoes can own a selected independent mip chain; new imports default to that choice. Global equipment rows offer All teams only. The beta-69 bounded native cache fill, HOME/AWAY lookup and field selector bind shoes10/Style 6 through separate clean and _mud rows; the earlier Style 3/shoes09 selector proof remains narrower; missing local names fall back to the newest loaded package. maumau78 reported a Style 6 Edit Player success and Bears in-game failure on beta 68; that report remains unresolved. Package, clean/mud state, roster transport and GPU visibility need a played retest. Original-size recognized retail artwork preserves its palette and complete mip chain, including legacy imports now compiled as an exact no-op. Unhonourable restored equipment groups are refused before publishing a loaded session. Fit refusals report measured byte shortfalls and offer a checked smaller-size retry when available. A smaller size and fewer shades lose detail. No larger-allocation option is shipped: chunk-loader growth alone does not prove archive relocation. Wrapper +0x14 and unselected sibling images remain exact. All current in-game outcomes are UNWITNESSED.",
